- Partner restrictions; or
- operational risk.
Where legally permitted, we will provide notice and reasons.In some circumstances, law may prohibit notice or detailed reasons.
Restrictions will be proportionate to the risk and legal requirement where Applicable Law requires proportionality.

You may close your Account subject to:
- settlement of pending transactions;
- repayment of outstanding debt;
- completion of required compliance checks;
- withdrawal or transfer of remaining eligible assets;
- legal retention obligations; and
- any Product Schedule governing investments, loans, custody or fixed - term products.
Closing an Account does not eliminate obligations that accrued before closure.

We may terminate or discontinue Services in accordance with Applicable Law.
Immediate termination may occur where permitted by law if:
- continued service would be unlawful;
- we reasonably suspect fraud or serious financial crime;
- you materially breach these Terms;
- you threaten the security of the platform or others;
- you use the Service for prohibited activity;
- required by a regulator, court or Partner; or
- we cannot complete legally required due diligence.
For ordinary commercial discontinuation, we will provide the notice required by Applicable Law and applicable Product Schedules.

After closure, we may:
- return eligible fiat funds to a verified bank or payment account;
- permit withdrawal of supported Digital Assets;
- transfer investments through an appropriate process;
- liquidate assets only where contractually authorized and legally permitted;
- deduct lawful outstanding amounts; or
- hold property as unclaimed property where required by law.
We may require completion of identity and security checks before releasing assets.

The insolvency treatment of your money, Digital Assets, securities or other property depends on:
- the legal entity providing the Service;
- whether assets are deposits, safeguarded funds, trust property, client assets, securities or general claims;
- whether segregation is legally effective;
- applicable custody structure;
- applicable deposit or investor compensation scheme; and
- governing insolvency law.
Product - specific disclosures will explain material insolvency protections where legally required.

You represent and warrant on an ongoing basis that:
1. information you provide is accurate and not misleading;
2. you have authority to use the Services;
3. funds and assets used with the Services are lawfully obtained;
4. you are not using the Services on behalf of an undisclosed person;
5. your use complies with Applicable Law;
6. you are not circumventing sanctions, geographic restrictions or product controls;
7. you will pay amounts validly owed; and
8. you will promptly notify us if any representation becomes materially inaccurate.

To the maximum extent permitted by Applicable Law, the Services are provided on an “as available” basis.
We do not warrant that:
- every Service will always be available;
- every transaction will be completed;
- every AI output will be accurate;
- third - party systems will remain available;
- Digital Asset networks will operate without interruption;
- market data will always be error - free; or
- the Services will meet every user’s particular purpose.
This clause does not exclude warranties or guarantees that cannot lawfully be excluded.

51.1 Non - excludable liability
