IMPORTANT IMPLEMENTATION NOTE — REMOVE BEFORE PUBLICATION:
These Terms are a comprehensive global template for a multi - product fintech platform involving payments, remittances, banking - like services, credit, lending, investments, blockchain / digital assets and AI - assisted functionality.They must be reviewed and localized by qualified counsel in every jurisdiction in which Nordi Remitwave operates or solicits customers.Do not publish statements implying that Nordi Remitwave is a licensed bank, lender, broker, investment adviser, custodian, money transmitter, payment institution, virtual - asset service provider or other regulated institution unless the relevant Nordi Remitwave entity actually holds that authorization.Product - specific disclosures, privacy notices, fee schedules, loan agreements, investment agreements, deposit disclosures and regulatory notices may also be legally required and should be incorporated by reference where appropriate.

1. ABOUT THESE TERMS
These Terms and Conditions(the “Terms”) govern access to and use of the websites, mobile applications, APIs, accounts, wallets, software, artificial - intelligence features, payment services, remittance services, credit and lending products, investment services, blockchain or digital - asset services, banking or banking - partner services, and other products or services made available under the Nordi Remitwave brand(collectively, the “Services”).
These Terms form a legally binding agreement between you and the Nordi Remitwave legal entity identified to you during onboarding, in your account, in a Product Schedule, or in a jurisdiction - specific disclosure(the “Company,” “Nordi Remitwave,” “we,” “us,” or “our”).
By opening an account, accessing or using any Service, clicking to accept these Terms, electronically signing an agreement that incorporates these Terms, or continuing to use a Service after a valid update takes effect, you agree to be bound by:
1. these Terms;
2. any applicable product - specific terms, loan agreement, cardholder agreement, custody agreement, investment agreement, staking terms, remittance disclosure, payment terms or other supplemental terms(each a “Product Schedule”);
3. our applicable fee schedule;
4. our Privacy Notice or Privacy Policy;
