7. AML, CFT, PROLIFERATION FINANCING, SANCTIONS AND FINANCIAL CRIME
7.1 Financial - crime controls
You acknowledge that we and our Partners may operate controls designed to prevent and detect:
- money laundering;
- terrorist financing;
- proliferation financing;
- sanctions evasion;
- bribery and corruption;
- fraud and scams;
- identity theft;
- tax evasion facilitation;
- market abuse;
- insider dealing;
- trafficking or exploitation;
- cybercrime;
- ransomware payments;
- theft or misappropriation of assets; and
- other unlawful activity.
7.2 Transaction monitoring
We may screen and monitor Accounts, counterparties, devices, wallets, IP addresses, transactions, blockchain addresses and behavioral patterns before, during and after transactions.
7.3 Delays, holds and restrictions
Where reasonably necessary to comply with Applicable Law, Partner requirements or financial - crime controls, we may:
- request further information or documents;
- delay, reject, reverse or block a transaction where legally permitted;
- place a hold on assets or funds;
- restrict withdrawals or transfers;
- suspend all or part of an Account;
- terminate a customer relationship;
- refuse to disclose certain information where disclosure is legally prohibited;
